{#
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE PROMO BAND — partials/promo-carousel.twig
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Ported from `handoff-new-pages/designs/ChallengeBanner.dc.html`. Mounted on five
  placements (account, nominate, home, vote, events) with `{% include %}` and a
  `placement` variable; the controller supplies `promos` from `PromoService`.

  TWO RULES FROM §4 THAT ARE NOT STYLE CHOICES

  · ZERO PROMOS RENDERS NOTHING. Not an empty band, not a placeholder — the markup is
    absent. A 188px strip of nothing on five pages is five pages with a hole in them.
  · ONE PROMO MEANS NO DOTS AND NO AUTO-ADVANCE. A carousel of one that still ticks is
    a thing that redraws itself for no reason, and dots that cannot change anything are
    controls that lie.

  AND ONE DEPARTURE FROM THE COMP, DELIBERATELY

  The comp pauses on hover and on `prefers-reduced-motion`. §4 also requires pausing on
  FOCUS-WITHIN, and it is right: WCAG 2.2.2 is about anything that moves for more than
  five seconds, and a keyboard user tabbing into a slide that then slides away loses
  what they were reading with no way to get it back. The script does both.

  The motion itself is CSS; the script only moves an index. So with JavaScript off this
  is a readable list of slides rather than a dead frame — see the `no-js` note below.
#}

{% if promos|default([])|length %}
  <section class="pb" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Challenges"
           {# `data-pb-count`, NOT `data-count`. `main.js` binds a GSAP count-up to
              every `[data-count]` on the page and writes the result into the element's
              `textContent` — which replaced this whole band with the character "0".
              Raw markup in the response, an empty band in the browser, and nothing in
              the console: an unnamespaced data attribute on a shared page is a global
              API, and this one already had an owner. #}
           data-ag-promos data-pb-count="{{ promos|length }}">

    <div class="pb__view">
      {#
        The track is sized in CSS from `--pb-n`, not from an inline width, so a slide
        count change needs no second place to keep true.
      #}
      <ul class="pb__track" style="--pb-n:{{ promos|length }}" data-pb-track>
        {% for p in promos %}
          <li class="pb__slide" data-theme="{{ p.theme }}"
              aria-roledescription="slide"
              aria-label="{{ loop.index }} of {{ promos|length }}: {{ p.title }}"
              {# Only the current slide is reachable. Without this a keyboard user tabs
                 into slides that are off-screen and the page scrolls sideways to
                 nothing — the commonest carousel fault there is. #}
              {% if not loop.first %}aria-hidden="true" inert{% endif %}>

            <span class="pb__deco" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="pb__ring"></span><span class="pb__disc"></span><span class="pb__dot"></span>
            </span>

            <span class="pb__body">
              {% if p.kicker or p.chip %}
                <span class="pb__kicker">
                  {{ p.kicker }}
                  {% if p.chip %}<span class="pb__chip" data-state="{{ p.chip_state }}">{{ p.chip }}</span>{% endif %}
                </span>
              {% endif %}
              <span class="pb__t">{{ p.title }}</span>
              {% if p.sub %}<span class="pb__s">{{ p.sub }}</span>{% endif %}
              <a class="pb__cta" href="{{ p.href }}"
                 {% if not loop.first %}tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>{{ p.cta }}</a>
            </span>

            {% if p.art %}
              {# Desktop only — the phone layout has no room and a 180px image beside
                 20px type is the title losing. `loading="lazy"` on all but the first:
                 the band is above the fold on the account page. #}
              <span class="pb__art" aria-hidden="true">
                <img src="{{ p.art }}" alt="" width="180" height="156"
                     loading="{{ loop.first ? 'eager' : 'lazy' }}" decoding="async">
              </span>
            {% endif %}
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>

    {% if promos|length > 1 %}
      <div class="pb__controls">
        {#
          32px targets, which is above the 24px AA floor and matches the comp. The
          visible pill is 8px (28px when current) and the hit area is the button.
        #}
        {% for p in promos %}
          <button class="pb__dot-btn" type="button" data-pb-go="{{ loop.index0 }}"
                  aria-label="Show slide {{ loop.index }} of {{ promos|length }}"
                  aria-current="{{ loop.first ? 'true' : 'false' }}">
            <span class="pb__pill"></span>
          </button>
        {% endfor %}

        {#
          WCAG 2.2.2 wants a mechanism to pause. It is a real button with a label that
          changes, not an icon alone — and it is rendered by the SERVER so it exists
          before any script runs.
        #}
        <button class="pb__pause" type="button" data-pb-pause aria-label="Pause slides">
          <svg class="pb__i-pause" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="2" y="1" width="3.5" height="12" rx="1"></rect>
            <rect x="8.5" y="1" width="3.5" height="12" rx="1"></rect>
          </svg>
          <svg class="pb__i-play" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M3 1.5v11l9-5.5z"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
{% endif %}
